    <string name="howto_done">Got it</string>
    <string name="howto_close_hint">Tap outside to close</string>
    <string name="howto_title_word">How to play: Word puzzle</string>
    <string name="howto_word_1">Find the hidden 5-letter word in 6 tries. Type a real word and press ENTER.</string>
    <string name="howto_word_2">After each try the letters change color: green is in the right place, yellow is in the word but in another place, gray is not in the word.</string>
    <string name="howto_word_3">Solve it to grow your streak. Running out of tries resets it.</string>
    <string name="howto_word_4">You can leave one unfinished puzzle per session with the skip. The language can only be changed before you start.</string>
    <string name="howto_title_memory">How to play: Memory match</string>
    <string name="howto_memory_1">Turn over two cards per move and find the 6 pairs.</string>
    <string name="howto_memory_2">Two cards with the same shape stay open. Different shapes are a mistake, and they turn back after a moment.</string>
    <string name="howto_memory_3">The 6th mistake loses the game. Finding every pair wins it.</string>
    <string name="howto_memory_4">Fewer moves and a faster time are better. The shapes are told apart by their form, not only their color.</string>
    <string name="howto_title_tubes">How to play: Color tubes</string>
    <string name="howto_tubes_1">Sort the colors until every tube holds one color only (or is empty).</string>
    <string name="howto_tubes_2">Tap a tube to lift it, then tap another tube to pour into it. The top color goes onto an empty tube, or onto the same color, as much as fits.</string>
    <string name="howto_tubes_3">There is no losing. If you get stuck, undo the last pour or restart the board. Your moves keep counting.</string>
    <string name="howto_tubes_4">Every color also has its own shape, so you can tell them apart without the colors.</string>
    <string name="howto_title_mines">How to play: Minesweeper</string>
    <string name="howto_mines_1">Open every cell that has no mine. Opening a mine loses the game.</string>
    <string name="howto_mines_2">A number tells how many mines touch that cell, diagonals too.</string>
    <string name="howto_mines_3">Tap to open a cell. Long-press to flag a cell you think is a mine, or turn on the flag button to flag with a tap.</string>
    <string name="howto_mines_4">Double-tap a number whose flags match it to open all the other cells around it at once. A wrong flag makes that lose.</string>
    <string name="howto_mines_5">Your first tap is always safe, and every board can be solved by logic alone, so you never have to guess.</string>
